TY  - RPRT
AU  - Torul, Orhan
TI  - Missionary Infrastructure and the Deepening of Ottoman State Schooling
PY  - 2026
UR  - https://orhantorul.com/research/def/
KW  - Educational competition
KW  - missionary schooling
KW  - state capacity
KW  - Ottoman Empire
KW  - administrative constraint
AB  - How did the Ottoman state expand schooling when confronted with rival foreign institutions? Using sanjak-level data for Anatolia (1876–1902/08), I estimate whether districts hosting American missionary main stations saw faster growth of male rüşdiye schools—the tier that trained provincial officials. Conditional on demographics, baseline schooling, and province indicators, station sanjaks added roughly one more school (control mean 1.9). The estimate is stable across reweighting, alternative rosters, and spatial falsification tests, but statistically insignificant under design-based inference (p = 0.15–0.31), reflecting 16 treated sanjaks in a 15-province sample. The pattern suggests defensive deepening in established hubs rather than frontier entry.
